<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lower Macedonia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lower Macedonia was the lowland core of the ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-macedon">Kingdom of Macedon</a>, the coastal plains around the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thermaic-gulf">Thermaic Gulf</a> watered by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haliacmon">Haliacmon</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vardar">Axios</a> rivers. It held the royal centres of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aigai">Aigai</a> and Pella and was the home of the Argead kings, who gradually brought the cantons of Upper Macedonia in the western mountains under their rule.</p></div>
